@*
    The #mapTilerKey island — a CREDENTIAL, deliberately not part of the settings payload.

    Rendered by the two pages whose entry actually reads it (overview/activities-page-init.ts and
    live-recording/live-recording.ts, both via core/map-api-key.setMapTilerApiKey). Details and Segment
    Statistics do NOT: they take the key from their own page-config islands, so the old shared partial was
    emitting an island neither of them read.

    Deliberately NOT moved into the layouts with the settings. Two reasons, both load-bearing:
      · /s/{token} is served to anyone with the URL. Share/View.cshtml passes IncludeMapTilerKey:false for
        exactly this reason, and a layout-level key island would hand the credential to every anonymous
        visitor — silently undoing that.
      · MapTilerService reads AppCredentials uncached, so putting it in a layout would add a DB round trip
        to every page in the app (R2). Two pages ask for it; two pages pay for it.

    Emits nothing when there is no key: TS reads '' and the keyless basemaps work.
*@
@model string?
@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model))
{
    <script type="application/json" id="mapTilerKey">@Html.Raw(BootstrapJson.Serialize(Model))</script>
}
